<title>SPAIN: PESETA DEBT/INTERBANK CLOSING REPORT.</title>
<headline>PESETA DEBT/INTERBANK CLOSING REPORT.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish government bonds were lifted on Tuesday at the close by Bunds, relieved that the Bundesbank set a fixed rate for its securities repurchase tender.</p>
<p>Traders had feared the German central bank would switch to a variable rate, leaving the door open for a rate hike to neutralise dollar strength against the mark. Dollar sluggishness surrounding the decision also buoyed bonos.</p>
<p>&quot;As we have no factors of our own, we are depending on the foreign markets,&quot; one analyst said. &quot;Now the markets are pretty quiet and the problems will return when the Bundesbank comes back from holidays&quot;.</p>
</text>
